sed volume within our California, Gulf Coast, Alaska, and North Texas regions, offset by decreases in sales in our Ohio River Valley, South Central, and Southwest regions.\nInnovative Pumping Solutions segment. Sales for the IPS segment increased $43.6 million, or 43.3 percent, for the three months ended September 30, 2026, compared to the prior year's corresponding period. This sales increase was the result of increases within our water and wastewater platform as well as strategic acquisitions within the IPS segment. Sales from recent acquisitions contributed $48.8 million during the period, compared to $6.7 million, for the three months ended September 30, 2025.\nSupply Chain Services segment. Sales for the SCS segment increased by $3.4 million, or 5.5 percent, for the three months ended September 30, 2026, compared to the prior year's corresponding period. This was primarily due to the onboarding of new customers and their related facilities as well as increased net activity with existing customers.\n"}
